# pnpm install-time supply-chain hardening.
#
# `minimum-release-age` (pnpm 10+) refuses to install any package
# version that's been on the registry for fewer than the configured
# number of MINUTES. Mitigates the class of attacks where a
# compromised maintainer publishes a malicious version and pulls it
# within hours — by the time we see it, it's either been caught and
# yanked, or it's old enough that signals (downloads, audits) are
# meaningful.
#
# Chosen value: 7 days = 10080 minutes. Matches the cooldown in
# .github/dependabot.yml (defence in depth — Dependabot won't even
# OFFER a fresh version PR, and direct `pnpm add` calls would be
# refused if they accidentally requested one).
#
# Tradeoff: legitimate hotfixes for security issues you actively
# wait for need a manual exemption. Override via the
# `minimum-release-age-exclude` allowlist (add a comma-separated
# list of package names below if/when you need one).
minimum-release-age=10080
